 # Plugins
 
+## Local prototype: card controls
+
+This checkout carries an unpublished extension, identified by `TESSERA_CARD_CONTROLS`.
+It also accepts `optional: true` on manifest inputs. The editor allows an empty value
+and offers the empty entity option again, so a selected slot can be cleared. Inputs
+without this field keep their required behaviour. Packages must supply defaults for
+missing optional values. The payload carries this flag to the editor.
+It does not claim a new upstream API version. During `Card::open`, register each child
+button with `tessera::ui::control(object, id)`. The host owns the LVGL event handler,
+rejects release outside the button, applies the shared touch guard and calls
+`Card::on_control(uint16_t id)`. IDs are local to a card. Re-registering an object
+replaces its previous registration. The host's normal deferred destruction protects
+callbacks that close their own card or open another. Plugins must not attach touch
+callbacks themselves. Stock Tessera does not provide this extension.
+
 A plugin adds something to the screens a person chooses, without the core knowing that plugin exists: a tile with data
 from a web service, hardware on one board, a feature not everyone needs. How to make one is in the plugins repository,
 [github.com/MaxGramser/tessera-plugins](https://github.com/MaxGramser/tessera-plugins) (its `docs/` and `AGENTS.md`).
